   "date": "2013-05-08T14:00:05Z",
   "subject": "Convergence problems cfa",
   "parts": [
    [
     1,
     "<font color=\"#000000\" size=\"3\" face=\"Times New Roman\">\r\n\r\n</font><p style=\"margin:0cm 0cm 10pt\" class=\"MsoNormal\"><span lang=\"EN-US\"><font size=\"3\"><font color=\"#000000\"><font face=\"Calibri\">Dear\r\nLavaan-users,<u></u><u></u><u></u></font></font></font></span></p><font color=\"#000000\" size=\"3\" face=\"Times New Roman\">\r\n\r\n</font><p style=\"margin:0cm 0cm 10pt\" class=\"MsoNormal\"><span lang=\"EN-US\"><font size=\"3\"><font color=\"#000000\"><font face=\"Calibri\">I recently\r\nstarted using lavaan, but encounter some convergence problems when trying to\r\nfit my models.<u></u><u></u></font></font></font></span></p><font color=\"#000000\" size=\"3\" face=\"Times New Roman\">\r\n\r\n</font><p style=\"margin:0cm 0cm 10pt\" class=\"MsoNormal\"><span lang=\"EN-US\"><font size=\"3\"><font color=\"#000000\"><font face=\"Calibri\">I have a\r\ndataset with scores between 0 and 5 of 783 participants on 15 variables. The scores\r\nare the sum of 5 very similar items (with correct=1, incorrect=0) on 15 different\r\nsubtests. I tread the scores as ordered given the limited range of possible\r\nvalues and skewness of the data. <u></u><u></u></font></font></font></span></p><font color=\"#000000\" size=\"3\" face=\"Times New Roman\">\r\n\r\n</font><p style=\"margin:0cm 0cm 10pt\" class=\"MsoNormal\"><span lang=\"EN-US\"><font face=\"Calibri\"><font size=\"3\"><font color=\"#000000\">I would\r\nlike to do a confirmatory factor analyses and have some alternative models to\r\ntest (I’ll<span>  </span>validate the final model on a\r\ndifferent data sample). Below, I show the model specifications. As you can see,\r\nnot all models use all variables, so for each model I take a subsample of the\r\ndata (mod1: 8 variables; mod2 and mod3: 13 variables).<u></u><u></u></font></font></font></span></p><font color=\"#000000\" size=\"3\" face=\"Times New Roman\">\r\n\r\n</font><p style=\"margin:0cm 0cm 10pt\" class=\"MsoNormal\"><span style=\"line-height:115%;font-family:&quot;Lucida Console&quot;;font-size:10pt\" lang=\"FR\"><font color=\"#000000\">mod1 &lt;- &#39;motion<span>  </span>=~ t6 + t9<span> \r\n</span>+ t11 + t12<u></u><u></u></font></span></p><font color=\"#000000\" size=\"3\" face=\"Times New Roman\">\r\n\r\n</font><p style=\"margin:0cm 0cm 10pt\" class=\"MsoNormal\"><font color=\"#000000\"><span style=\"line-height:115%;font-family:&quot;Lucida Console&quot;;font-size:10pt\" lang=\"FR\"><span>         </span></span><span style=\"line-height:115%;font-family:&quot;Lucida Console&quot;;font-size:10pt\" lang=\"EN-US\">meaning =~ t9 + t10 + t13 + t15<u></u><u></u></span></font></p><font color=\"#000000\" size=\"3\" face=\"Times New Roman\">\r\n\r\n</font><p style=\"margin:0cm 0cm 10pt\" class=\"MsoNormal\"><span style=\"line-height:115%;font-family:&quot;Lucida Console&quot;;font-size:10pt\" lang=\"EN-US\"><font color=\"#000000\"><span>         </span>color<span>  \r\n</span>=~ t5 + t10 + t13 + t15&#39;<u></u><u></u></font></span></p><font color=\"#000000\" size=\"3\" face=\"Times New Roman\">\r\n\r\n</font><p style=\"margin:0cm 0cm 10pt\" class=\"MsoNormal\"><span style=\"line-height:115%;font-family:&quot;Lucida Console&quot;;font-size:10pt\" lang=\"FR\"><font color=\"#000000\">mod2 &lt;- &#39;grouping<span>      </span>=~ t2 + t3 + t6 + t7 + t8 + t9 + t11 +\r\nt12 + t14<u></u><u></u></font></span></p><font color=\"#000000\" size=\"3\" face=\"Times New Roman\">\r\n\r\n</font><p style=\"margin:0cm 0cm 10pt\" class=\"MsoNormal\"><span style=\"line-height:115%;font-family:&quot;Lucida Console&quot;;font-size:10pt\" lang=\"FR\"><font color=\"#000000\"><span>        </span>segmentation<span>  </span>=~ t3 + t5 + t6 + t7 + t11 + t14 + t15<u></u><u></u></font></span></p><font color=\"#000000\" size=\"3\" face=\"Times New Roman\">\r\n\r\n</font><p style=\"margin:0cm 0cm 10pt\" class=\"MsoNormal\"><span style=\"line-height:115%;font-family:&quot;Lucida Console&quot;;font-size:10pt\" lang=\"FR\"><font color=\"#000000\"><span>        </span>figure_ground =~ t3 + t5 + t6 + t7<u></u><u></u></font></span></p><font color=\"#000000\" size=\"3\" face=\"Times New Roman\">\r\n\r\n</font><p style=\"margin:0cm 0cm 10pt\" class=\"MsoNormal\"><span style=\"line-height:115%;font-family:&quot;Lucida Console&quot;;font-size:10pt\" lang=\"FR\"><font color=\"#000000\"><span>        </span>shape<span>         </span>=~ t1 + t3 + t4 + t5 + t6 + t7 + t8 +\r\nt14&#39;<u></u><u></u></font></span></p><font color=\"#000000\" size=\"3\" face=\"Times New Roman\">\r\n\r\n</font><p style=\"margin:0cm 0cm 10pt\" class=\"MsoNormal\"><span style=\"line-height:115%;font-family:&quot;Lucida Console&quot;;font-size:10pt\" lang=\"FR\"><font color=\"#000000\">mod3 &lt;-\r\n&#39;spatial_relations =~ t1 + t2 + t3 + t4 + t5 + t7 + t8 + t9 + t10 + t11 +t14<u></u><u></u></font></span></p><font color=\"#000000\" size=\"3\" face=\"Times New Roman\">\r\n\r\n</font><p style=\"margin:0cm 0cm 10pt\" class=\"MsoNormal\"><span style=\"line-height:115%;font-family:&quot;Lucida Console&quot;;font-size:10pt\" lang=\"FR\"><font color=\"#000000\"><span>        </span>fine_details<span>      </span>=~ t1 + t2 + t3 + t4 + t7 + t8<u></u><u></u></font></span></p><font color=\"#000000\" size=\"3\" face=\"Times New Roman\">\r\n\r\n</font><p style=\"margin:0cm 0cm 10pt\" class=\"MsoNormal\"><span style=\"line-height:115%;font-family:&quot;Lucida Console&quot;;font-size:10pt\" lang=\"FR\"><font color=\"#000000\"><span>        </span>cue_invariance<span>    </span>=~ t3 + t5 + t6 + t7 + t8 <u></u><u></u></font></span></p><font color=\"#000000\" size=\"3\" face=\"Times New Roman\">\r\n\r\n</font><p style=\"margin:0cm 0cm 10pt\" class=\"MsoNormal\"><span style=\"line-height:115%;font-family:&quot;Lucida Console&quot;;font-size:10pt\" lang=\"FR\"><font color=\"#000000\"><span>        </span>shape_invariance<span>  </span>=~ t1 + t3 + t7 +t8&#39;<u></u><u></u></font></span></p><font color=\"#000000\" size=\"3\" face=\"Times New Roman\">\r\n\r\n</font><p style=\"margin:0cm 0cm 10pt\" class=\"MsoNormal\"><span lang=\"EN-US\"><font size=\"3\"><font color=\"#000000\"><font face=\"Calibri\">I estimate\r\nthe models with the following statements:<u></u><u></u></font></font></font></span></p><font color=\"#000000\" size=\"3\" face=\"Times New Roman\">\r\n\r\n</font><p style=\"margin:0cm 0cm 10pt\" class=\"MsoNormal\"><span style=\"line-height:115%;font-family:&quot;Lucida Console&quot;;font-size:10pt\" lang=\"FR\"><font color=\"#000000\">fit1&lt;-cfa(mod1,\r\ndata=cfa_subtests_data1, ordered=c(&quot;t5&quot;,&quot;t6&quot;,&quot;t9&quot;,&quot;t10&quot;,&quot;t11&quot;,&quot;t12&quot;,&quot;t13&quot;,&quot;t15&quot;)\r\n)<u></u><u></u></font></span></p><font color=\"#000000\" size=\"3\" face=\"Times New Roman\">\r\n\r\n</font><p style=\"margin:0cm 0cm 10pt\" class=\"MsoNormal\"><span style=\"line-height:115%;font-family:&quot;Lucida Console&quot;;font-size:10pt\" lang=\"FR\"><font color=\"#000000\">fit2&lt;-cfa(mod2,\r\ndata=cfa_subtests_data2, ordered=c(&quot;t1&quot;,&quot;t2&quot;,\r\n&quot;t3&quot;,\r\n&quot;t4&quot;,&quot;t5&quot;,&quot;t6&quot;,&quot;t7&quot;,&quot;t8&quot;,&quot;t9&quot;,&quot;t11&quot;,&quot;t12&quot;,&quot;t14&quot;,&quot;t15&quot;)\r\n)<u></u><u></u></font></span></p><font color=\"#000000\" size=\"3\" face=\"Times New Roman\">\r\n\r\n</font><p style=\"margin:0cm 0cm 10pt\" class=\"MsoNormal\"><span style=\"line-height:115%;font-family:&quot;Lucida Console&quot;;font-size:10pt\" lang=\"FR\"><font color=\"#000000\">fit3&lt;-cfa(mod3,\r\ndata=cfa_subtests_data3, ordered=c(&quot;t1&quot;,&quot;t2&quot;,\r\n&quot;t3&quot;,\r\n&quot;t4&quot;,&quot;t5&quot;,&quot;t6&quot;,&quot;t7&quot;,&quot;t8&quot;,&quot;t9&quot;,&quot;t10&quot;,&quot;t11&quot;,&quot;t14&quot;)\r\n)<u></u><u></u></font></span></p><font color=\"#000000\" size=\"3\" face=\"Times New Roman\">\r\n\r\n</font><p style=\"margin:0cm 0cm 10pt\" class=\"MsoNormal\"><span lang=\"EN-US\"><font size=\"3\"><font color=\"#000000\"><font face=\"Calibri\">None of\r\nthese models reach convergence. I always get this error message:<u></u><u></u></font></font></font></span></p><font color=\"#000000\" size=\"3\" face=\"Times New Roman\">\r\n\r\n</font><p style=\"margin:0cm 0cm 0pt;line-height:normal\" class=\"MsoNormal\"><span style=\"color:rgb(197,6,11);font-family:&quot;Lucida Console&quot;;font-size:10pt\" lang=\"EN-US\">lavaan WARNING: model has NOT converged!</span><span style=\"background:rgb(225,226,229);color:black;font-family:&quot;Lucida Console&quot;;font-size:10pt\" lang=\"EN-US\"><u></u><u></u></span></p><font color=\"#000000\" size=\"3\" face=\"Times New Roman\">\r\n\r\n</font><p style=\"margin:0cm 0cm 10pt\" class=\"MsoNormal\"><span lang=\"EN-US\"><u></u><font color=\"#000000\" size=\"3\" face=\"Calibri\"> </font><u></u></span></p><font color=\"#000000\" size=\"3\" face=\"Times New Roman\">\r\n\r\n</font><p style=\"margin:0cm 0cm 10pt\" class=\"MsoNormal\"><span lang=\"EN-US\"><font face=\"Calibri\"><font size=\"3\"><font color=\"#000000\">Simplifying\r\n<span> </span>the models by removing one factor of by\r\nchanging the latent variable definition does not seem to help. At the best I\r\nget my estimates but with this warning:<u></u><u></u></font></font></font></span></p><font color=\"#000000\" size=\"3\" face=\"Times New Roman\">\r\n\r\n</font><pre><font size=\"2\"><span><span style=\"background:rgb(225,226,229);color:rgb(197,6,11);font-family:&quot;Lucida Console&quot;\" lang=\"EN-US\">lavaan WARNING: covariance matrix of latent variables is not positive definite</span></span><span style=\"background:rgb(225,226,229);color:black;font-family:&quot;Lucida Console&quot;\" lang=\"EN-US\"><u></u><u></u></span></font></pre><font color=\"#000000\" size=\"3\" face=\"Times New Roman\">\r\n\r\n</font><p style=\"margin:0cm 0cm 10pt\" class=\"MsoNormal\"><span lang=\"EN-US\"><u></u><font color=\"#000000\" size=\"3\" face=\"Calibri\"> </font><u></u></span></p><font color=\"#000000\" size=\"3\" face=\"Times New Roman\">\r\n\r\n\r\n\r\n</font><p style=\"margin:0cm 0cm 10pt\" class=\"MsoNormal\"><b><span lang=\"EN-US\"><font size=\"3\"><font color=\"#000000\"><font face=\"Calibri\">Is this a problem in my model specifications or\r\nis my model not identifiable? How could this be solved?<u></u><u></u></font></font></font></span></b></p><font color=\"#000000\" size=\"3\" face=\"Times New Roman\">\r\n\r\n</font><p style=\"margin:0cm 0cm 10pt\" class=\"MsoNormal\"><span lang=\"EN-US\"><font size=\"3\"><font color=\"#000000\"><font face=\"Calibri\">Also, a\r\ncouple of months ago I performed a similar analysis with lavaan 0.5-11 and this\r\nworked fine, but since I updated to lavaan 0.5-12 I get a warning that the\r\ncovariance matrix is not positive definite with exactly the same code. Could\r\nthis be related to the convergence problems I experience now? My code for the\r\nthis similar analysis is:<u></u><u></u></font></font></font></span></p><font color=\"#000000\" size=\"3\" face=\"Times New Roman\">\r\n\r\n</font><p style=\"margin:0cm 0cm 10pt\" class=\"MsoNormal\"><span style=\"line-height:115%;font-family:&quot;Lucida Console&quot;;font-size:10pt\" lang=\"FR\"><font color=\"#000000\">cfamodel1 &lt;- &#39;Grouping <span> </span>=~ t2 + t6 + t9 + t11+ t12<u></u><u></u></font></span></p><font color=\"#000000\" size=\"3\" face=\"Times New Roman\">\r\n\r\n</font><p style=\"margin:0cm 0cm 10pt\" class=\"MsoNormal\"><span style=\"line-height:115%;font-family:&quot;Lucida Console&quot;;font-size:10pt\" lang=\"FR\"><font color=\"#000000\"><span>      </span><span> </span><span>     </span>Figureground=~ t3 + t5 + t7 +t8 + t13 + t15<u></u><u></u></font></span></p><font color=\"#000000\" size=\"3\" face=\"Times New Roman\">\r\n\r\n</font><p style=\"margin:0cm 0cm 10pt 35.4pt;text-indent:35.4pt\" class=\"MsoNormal\"><span style=\"line-height:115%;font-family:&quot;Lucida Console&quot;;font-size:10pt\" lang=\"FR\"><font color=\"#000000\">GlobalLocal<span> </span>=~ t10 +\r\nt14<u></u><u></u></font></span></p><font color=\"#000000\" size=\"3\" face=\"Times New Roman\">\r\n\r\n</font><p style=\"margin:0cm 0cm 10pt 35.4pt;text-indent:35.4pt\" class=\"MsoNormal\"><span style=\"line-height:115%;font-family:&quot;Lucida Console&quot;;font-size:10pt\" lang=\"FR\"><font color=\"#000000\">ShapeDiscr<span>  </span>=~ t1 + t4&#39;<u></u><u></u></font></span></p><font color=\"#000000\" size=\"3\" face=\"Times New Roman\">\r\n\r\n</font><p style=\"margin:0cm 0cm 10pt\" class=\"MsoNormal\"><span style=\"line-height:115%;font-family:&quot;Lucida Console&quot;;font-size:10pt\" lang=\"FR\"><font color=\"#000000\">fit &lt;- cfa(cfamodel1,\r\ndata=subtest.data, ordered=c(&#39;t1&#39;, &#39;t2&#39;, &#39;t3&#39;, &#39;t4&#39;, &#39;t5&#39;, &#39;t6&#39;, &#39;t7&#39;, &#39;t8&#39;, t9&#39;,\r\n&#39;t10&#39;, &#39;t11&#39;, &#39;t12&#39;, &#39;t13&#39;,&#39;t14&#39;, &#39;t15&#39;))<u></u><u></u></font></span></p><font color=\"#000000\" size=\"3\" face=\"Times New Roman\">\r\n\r\n</font><p style=\"margin:0cm 0cm 10pt\" class=\"MsoNormal\"><span lang=\"EN-US\"><font size=\"3\"><font color=\"#000000\"><font face=\"Calibri\">I use R\r\n2.15 with lavaan 0.5-12. If you need any other information, please let me know.<u></u><u></u></font></font></font></span></p><font color=\"#000000\" size=\"3\" face=\"Times New Roman\">\r\n\r\n</font><p style=\"margin:0cm 0cm 10pt\" class=\"MsoNormal\"><span lang=\"EN-US\"><font size=\"3\"><font color=\"#000000\"><font face=\"Calibri\">Any help\r\nwould he highly appreciated.<u></u><u></u></font></font></font></span></p><font color=\"#000000\" size=\"3\" face=\"Times New Roman\">\r\n\r\n</font><p style=\"margin:0cm 0cm 10pt\" class=\"MsoNormal\"><span lang=\"EN-US\"><u></u><font color=\"#000000\" size=\"3\" face=\"Calibri\"> </font><u></u></span></p><font color=\"#000000\" size=\"3\" face=\"Times New Roman\">\r\n\r\n</font><p style=\"margin:0cm 0cm 10pt\" class=\"MsoNormal\"><span lang=\"EN-US\"><font size=\"3\"><font color=\"#000000\"><font face=\"Calibri\">Kind\r\nregards,<u></u><u></u></font></font></font></span></p><font color=\"#000000\" size=\"3\" face=\"Times New Roman\">\r\n\r\n</font><p style=\"margin:0cm 0cm 10pt\" class=\"MsoNormal\"><span lang=\"EN-US\"><font size=\"3\"><font color=\"#000000\"><font face=\"Calibri\">Kathleen\r\nVancleef<u></u><u></u></font></font></font></span></p><font color=\"#000000\" size=\"3\" face=\"Times New Roman\">\r\n\r\n</font>"
    ]
   ]
  },
  {
   "id": "EcKumNOURmEJ",
   "from": "yrosseel",
   "author": "89c9fc822e34b78c",
   "date": "2013-05-08T17:12:40Z",
   "subject": "Re: Convergence problems cfa",
   "parts": [
    [
     2,
     "On 05/08/2013 04:00 PM, <a href data-email-masked rel=\"nofollow\">kathleen...@psy.kuleuven.be</a> wrote:\r<br>&gt; Dear Lavaan-users,\r<br>&gt;\r<br>&gt; I recently started using lavaan, but encounter some convergence problems\r<br>&gt; when trying to fit my models.\r<br>&gt;\r<br>&gt; I have a dataset with scores between 0 and 5 of 783 participants on 15\r<br>&gt; variables. The scores are the sum of 5 very similar items (with\r<br>&gt; correct=1, incorrect=0) on 15 different subtests. I tread the scores as\r<br>&gt; ordered given the limited range of possible values and skewness of the\r<br>&gt; data.\r<br>\r<br>"
    ],
    [
     1,
     "You could also try treating the variables as continuous, and use \r<br>estimator &quot;MLR&quot; (to handle skewness).\r<br>"
    ],
    [
     2,
     "\r<br>&gt; lavaan WARNING: model has NOT converged!\r<br>\r<br>"
    ],
    [
     1,
     "At first sight, the problem seems to be that there is too much overlap \r<br>between the factors (too many shared items). I think you need at least 2 \r<br>indicators per factor that are unique (ie zero loadings on all other \r<br>factors).\r<br>"
    ],
    [
     2,
     "\r<br>&gt; lavaan WARNING: covariance matrix of latent variables is not positive definite\r<br>\r<br>"
    ],
    [
     1,
     "If you get this warning, try this:\r<br>\r<br>eigen(inspect(fit, &quot;<a href=\"http://cov.lv\" target=\"_blank\" rel=\"nofollow\" data-saferedirecturl=\"https://www.google.com/url?hl=en-US&amp;q=http://cov.lv&amp;source=gmail&amp;ust=1792432900223000&amp;usg=AOvVaw28WRdpy-M0B4uQuophAv1c\">cov.lv</a>&quot;))$values\r<br>\r<br>If the last value is very, very close to zero (say, -1e-015), you can \r<br>safely ignore this. This check is rather &#39;strict&#39;, and will be relaxed a \r<br>little bit in the next version.\r<br>"
    ],
    [
     2,
     "\r<br>&gt; Also, a couple of months ago I performed a similar analysis with lavaan\r<br>&gt; 0.5-11 and this worked fine, but since I updated to lavaan 0.5-12 I get\r<br>&gt; a warning that the covariance matrix is not positive definite with\r<br>&gt; exactly the same code.\r<br>\r<br>"
    ],
    [
     1,
     "This is just a new check added in 0.5-12. A bit too strict perhaps.\r<br>\r<br>Yves.\r<br>\r<br>"
    ]
   ]
  },
  {
   "id": "cYXtqF9FaeAJ",
